<title>POLAND: Poland prices KGHM institutional offer at PLN 21.0.</title>
<headline>Poland prices KGHM institutional offer at PLN 21.0.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish treasury ministry set the final strike price in the institutional offer of its KGHM Polska Miedz SA copper concern at 21.0 zlotys per share, the offering's domestic manager said on Saturday.</p>
<p>The minimum price for the institutional offer was set at 19.5 zlotys. The treasury ministry also increased the retail domestic offer by 10 million shares from the original six million shares.  </p>
<p>    Issuer:				KGHM Polska Miedz SA</p>
<p> Type of issue:			  existing common shares</p>
<p> Priced at (PLN):			21.0</p>
<p> minimum instutional price	   19.5</p>
<p>    final retail price		 19.0</p>
<p> (Previous) Pricing Range:	   18-23</p>
<p> No of Shares Offered:		 55,000,000-72,000,000</p>
<p> No of Existing Shares:		200,000,000</p>
<p> Lead Manager:			   United Bank of Switzerland</p>
<p>					     Barclays de Zoete Wedd</p>
<p> Domestic Manager:		     WBK SA brokerage</p>
<p> Lead Underwriter:		     To be announced</p>
<p> Issue Purpose:			  facilitate privatisation</p>
<p> Tranches		     No of Shares	   Subscription</p>
<p>				  Offered		  Period</p>
<p> Domestic Small-Investor 16,000,000	     June 30-July 4</p>
<p> Domestic Large-Investor 14,000,000	     June 30-July 4</p>
<p> International Tranche   35,000,000</p>
<p>  (book building)				     June 23-July 3</p>
<p>NOTES: - Domestic retail tranche has been increased by 10,000,000 shares. An additional seven million shares may be issued by global coordinators as GDRs.</p>
<p>- Institutional offer to be allotted on July 5 and July 6.</p>
<p>- The entire international tranche will be issued in global depositary receipts (GDRs).</p>
<p>- Up to 15 percent of KGHM shares reserved for employees.</p>
<p>Earnings Data (million PLN)  1997 forecast	  1996</p>
<p> Net profit:		  286.0		    147.2</p>
<p> Operating profit:	  511.0		    390.3</p>
<p> Sales:		     3,683.0		  3,351.0</p>
<p> Group net profit:	  310.0		    148.9</p>
<p> Group operating:	   528.0		    387.3</p>
<p> Group sales:	     3,883.0		  3,527.2</p>
<p>Main Shareholders: State treasury - 100 pct of shares.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
